We keep the rest of the policy as you proposed:

"Each fisher may take a maximum of 3 kg per trip, and the community’s total monthly harvest may not exceed 6 % of the lake’s current stock. Fishing days are rotated so that at most one fisher is on the lake per day. The council meets on the 1st day of each month, reviews the previous month’s recorded totals and the updated lake stock, and then adjusts the 6 % cap accordingly for the next month. Any fisher who exceeds the 3 kg per‑trip limit or the monthly cap must surrender excess catch and faces a 30‑day ban."","revised_policy":"Each fisher may take a maximum of 3 kg per trip, and the community’s total monthly harvest may not exceed 6 % of the lake’s current stock. Fishing days are rotated so that at most one fisher is on the lake per day. The council meets on the 1st day of each month, reviews the previous month’s recorded totals and the updated lake stock, and then adjusts the 6 % cap accordingly for the next month. Any fisher who exceeds the 3 kg per‑trip limit or the monthly cap must surrender excess catch and faces a 30‑day ban.","revised_operationalization":"No change to operationalization.","reasoning":"I explained the council’s method for handling excess catch, which satisfies the question while keeping the existing policy and operational details unchanged."}

