{"answer":"I’m the one who will keep the pool in a communal ledger. Every month we’ll pick a fisherman (rotating, so no one person owns it all) to write down all the fish that go into the pool. After the last trip of the month, we’ll gather, read the ledger, and split the total amount of fish in the pool equally among all fishers whose reserves are below 15 kg. Each fisherman will then receive that share in the next trip and we’ll update the ledger. That way everyone knows how much is in the pool and who gets it.

The policy stays the same:

"Each fisher may keep up to 5 kg per trip; any fish caught beyond 5 kg is added to a communal pool that is redistributed monthly to fishers whose reserves are below 15 kg, capped at 2 kg per fisher per month. Before each trip, every fisher records his current reserve. If a fisher’s reserve is under 10 kg, he must set aside 0.5 kg of his catch for the pool (in addition to the 5 kg limit). After all trips in a month, the pool is summed and divided equally among all fishers whose reserves are below 15 kg. Fishers who fail to adhere to the 5 kg limit or the 0.5 kg contribution when required must forfeit 1 kg of their catch that month, which is added to the pool."","revised_policy":""Each fisher may keep up to 5 kg per trip; any fish caught beyond 5 kg is added to a communal pool that is redistributed monthly to fishers whose reserves are below 15 kg, capped at 2 kg per fisher per month. Before each trip, every fisher records his current reserve. If a fisher’s reserve is under 10 kg, he must set aside 0.5 kg of his catch for the pool (in addition to the 5 kg limit). After all trips in a month, the pool is summed and divided equally among all fishers whose reserves are below 15 kg. Fishers who fail to adhere to the 5 kg limit or the 0.5 kg contribution when required must forfeit 1 kg of their catch that month, which is added to the pool."","revised_operationalization":"A rotating fisherman each month will act as the pool custodian, keeping a communal ledger of all fish added to the pool. At the end of the month, after all trips, the total pool will be summed and split equally among all fishers whose reserves are below 15 kg. Each fisher will receive his share in the next trip, and the ledger will be updated to reflect the distribution.","reasoning":"I wanted to make sure the pool is managed transparently and fairly, so I added a rotating custodian and a clear monthly distribution process."}

